  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Clean Energy for Climate-Smart Schools in Viet Nam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GGGI, in partnership with UNICEF, has joint developed the project &#x201c;Clean Energy for Climate-Smart Schools in Viet Nam&#x201d;. This one-year project will conduct the market study to explore potential landscape of solar rooftop for the education sector in Viet Nam as well the market appetite of various stakeholders on RTS investment in schools in Vietnam. Additionally, it will assess possible financing options that would incentivize schools and the private sector to invest in RTS, catalyzed by public finance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to identify the potential landscape of solar rooftop for the education sector in Vietnam, Additionally, the project aims to identify blended financial mechanisms to address the financial limitation and scale-up RTS in schools. The implementation of RTS in schools in the country will not only provide additional energy resource, but also contribute to raising awareness of children in using clean energy.</narrative>
  </description>
